{"title":"Detecting Colour and Monochrome Monitors","slug":"Detecting_Colour_and_Monochrome_Monitors","html":"<p>Detecting whether a user has a colour or monochrome video card is a trivial task. The <a data-wiki=\"BIOS\" href=\"#/library/BIOS\">BIOS</a> <a data-wiki=\"Memory Map (x86)\" href=\"#/library/Memory_Map_x86/bios_data_area_bda\">data segment</a> has a value in it for this information. Below is a function (in ISO C) to retrieve this:</p>\n<h2 id=\"the_function\">The Function</h2>\n<div class=\"sourceCode\" id=\"cb1\"><pre class=\"sourceCode c\"><code class=\"sourceCode c\"><span id=\"cb1-1\"><span class=\"pp\">#include </span><span class=\"im\">&lt;stdint.h&gt;</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-2\"></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-3\"><span class=\"kw\">enum</span> video_type</span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-4\"><span class=\"op\">{</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-5\">    VIDEO_TYPE_NONE <span class=\"op\">=</span> <span class=\"bn\">0x00</span><span class=\"op\">,</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-6\">    VIDEO_TYPE_COLOUR <span class=\"op\">=</span> <span class=\"bn\">0x20</span><span class=\"op\">,</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-7\">    VIDEO_TYPE_MONOCHROME <span class=\"op\">=</span> <span class=\"bn\">0x30</span><span class=\"op\">,</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-8\"><span class=\"op\">};</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-9\"></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-10\"><span class=\"dt\">uint16_t</span> detect_bios_area_hardware<span class=\"op\">(</span><span class=\"dt\">void</span><span class=\"op\">)</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-11\"><span class=\"op\">{</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-12\">    <span class=\"dt\">const</span> <span class=\"dt\">uint16_t</span><span class=\"op\">*</span> bda_detected_hardware_ptr <span class=\"op\">=</span> <span class=\"op\">(</span><span class=\"dt\">const</span> <span class=\"dt\">uint16_t</span><span class=\"op\">*)</span> <span class=\"bn\">0x410</span><span class=\"op\">;</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-13\">    <span class=\"cf\">return</span> <span class=\"op\">*</span>bda_detected_hardware_ptr<span class=\"op\">;</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-14\"><span class=\"op\">}</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-15\"></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-16\"><span class=\"kw\">enum</span> video_type get_bios_area_video_type<span class=\"op\">(</span><span class=\"dt\">void</span><span class=\"op\">)</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-17\"><span class=\"op\">{</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-18\">    <span class=\"cf\">return</span> <span class=\"op\">(</span><span class=\"kw\">enum</span> video_type<span class=\"op\">)</span> <span class=\"op\">(</span>detect_bios_area_hardware<span class=\"op\">()</span> <span class=\"op\">&amp;</span> <span class=\"bn\">0x30</span><span class=\"op\">);</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-19\"><span class=\"op\">}</span></span></code></pre></div>\n","toc":[{"id":"the_function","text":"The Function","level":2}],"categories":["Hardware Detection","Video"],"rating":null,"flags":[],"words":98,"summary":"Detecting whether a user has a colour or monochrome video card is a trivial task. The BIOS data segment has a value in it for this information. Below is a function (in ISO C) to retrieve this:","updated":"2023-07-09","authors":["Khaledhammouda"],"url":"https://wiki.osdev.org/Detecting_Colour_and_Monochrome_Monitors","history":"https://wiki.osdev.org/index.php?title=Detecting_Colour_and_Monochrome_Monitors&action=history","backlinks":[{"t":"Printing To Screen","s":"Printing_To_Screen"}],"lessons":[{"id":"t12m2l3","title":"Deep dive: VGA hardware","kind":"further"}]}